1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,063
Insect neurons are cheap, sensitive, and
already used as biosensors.

2
00:00:07,113 --> 00:00:12,084
Everyone asks how early one neuron can
warn you.

3
00:00:12,134 --> 00:00:21,603
Nobody asks the deployment question: how many do you need, where, and how should
they vote?

4
00:00:21,653 --> 00:00:24,950
That is what this study answers.

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:33,718
The only empirical input is real:
gamma-renewal fits to sixteen cockroach
and locust units from two open Zenodo
datasets.

6
00:00:33,768 --> 00:00:49,805
Around them we simulate a toxic front
spreading at one and a half units per
second, sensors on a grid, at random, or
clustered, one-second spike counts with
measurement noise, and three detectors
times three network rules.

7
00:00:49,855 --> 00:00:54,950
Every pipeline is calibrated to the same
false-alarm rate on null runs.

8
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:56,604
Here is one run.

9
00:00:56,654 --> 00:01:03,219
Sixteen sensors on a grid, CUSUM with
nearest-neighbour pooling.

10
00:01:03,269 --> 00:01:19,446
The source collapses at sixty-six seconds;
the network alarms at sixty, six seconds
early, and places the source within eight
percent of the domain diagonal.

11
00:01:19,496 --> 00:01:31,436
The full study repeats this fifty-four times over sensor count, layout and noise,
twenty seeds each, nine pipelines.

12
00:01:31,486 --> 00:01:34,950
One command reproduces everything.

13
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:35,865
Three results.

14
00:01:35,915 --> 00:01:48,479
First, pooling beats every other rule:
seventy-five percent detection and about
seven seconds of lead on average, versus
sixty-three percent for the naive max rule
at the same false-alarm rate.

15
00:01:48,529 --> 00:02:00,767
Second, layout matters as much as count:
sixteen grid sensors reach ninety-five
percent detection; random placement needs
thirty-six; clustered placement never
reaches one hundred percent.

16
00:02:00,817 --> 00:02:06,649
Third, a warning: the max rule collapses as you add sensors when the statistic is
bounded.

17
00:02:06,699 --> 00:02:12,728
BOCPD-plus-max drops from eighty to ten percent detection between nine and a
hundred sensors.

18
00:02:12,778 --> 00:02:14,950
Pooled BOCPD stays at one hundred.

19
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:34,950
The simulator is also an MCP server, so a
research agent can run its own sweeps and
get back the same numbers the command line
produces.

20
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:39,950
What this is not: the front, the decay and
the collapse endpoint are simulated.

21
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:43,684
This is a network-design study, not a
biological lead time.

22
00:02:43,734 --> 00:02:45,266
Rate is the only feature.

23
00:02:45,316 --> 00:02:49,950
Next is validation on recordings with a
real pharmacological intervention.

24
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:56,924
Code, data pipeline and the one-page
abstract are in the repository.

25
00:02:56,974 --> 00:02:57,950
Thank you.

